00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.990
Film Courage: How did you learn to write a
feature-length script?  Peter Dukes, Writer/Director: Yeah I never went

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:09.719
to any master programs I never went to
any film programs that specifically

00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:15.719
taught me my craft as I'd mentioned CU [University of Colorado Boulder]
was more about film theory and various

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:21.029
things like that it didn't really teach
me in great depth what you need to do as

00:00:21.029 --> 00:00:25.500
a director or writer I had to learn all
that on my own whether I did it right or

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.510
wrong who's to say but for me is that it
looted to you before I just wrote and

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:35.820
wrote and wrote and wrote and through
all that writing through all those years

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.829
you start to find your own voice and
when I wasn't writing I was reading

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:45.180
again great scripts different kinds of
scripts the more type of scripts the

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:51.270
better any different styles you know you
never want to get attached to one

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:55.710
person's style that he might start to
emulate it I mean read different styles

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.710
and go gosh this is amazing I never
thought you could do it this way and

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:04.049
what I eventually earned learned through
the years is is when I'm writing my

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:09.030
scripts I don't just want to write a
scene or write a story

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:14.070
I bring literally the words the
structure of the sentences themselves to

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:17.670
life I break things apart certain
descriptions certain ways I do it

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:22.439
depending on the project it should be an
experience to read it and it should be

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:27.930
something that literally pulls the
reader from one page to the next where

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:32.880
they can't stop if your script doesn't
hook the reader on the first page you're

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:38.009
done that's just the realities is a lot
of agents and managers will joke well

00:01:38.009 --> 00:01:42.390
I'll give you the old five page rule
there was the rule of thumb some say ten

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.930
